WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.692
Null values still mean what they meant earlier in the course.

00:00:03.692 --> 00:00:07.082
A null value is not automatically zero.

00:00:07.082 --> 00:00:13.078
It is not the same as an empty string, and it is not the same as a placeholder such as unknown.

00:00:13.686 --> 00:00:18.498
This matters even more when a transformation is running across millions of rows.

00:00:18.498 --> 00:00:23.133
A small mistake in null handling can affect a very large output.

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:30.773
Keep the Module 9 habit: decide what missingness means, standardize it only when the business rule is clear,

00:00:30.773 --> 00:00:32.357
and validate the result.
